description:
In repos/goal-host-vessel/src/index.ts, let the compute-artifact oracle resolve a memory-note title that the operator did not put in quotation marks.

Replace these six consecutive lines, which occur exactly once in the file:
  if (!title) return null;
  try {
    const res = await fetch(`${DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT}/resolve`, {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", ...(API_KEY ? { Authorization: `ApiKey ${API_KEY}` } : {}) },
      body: JSON.stringify({ pointer: { type: "memoryNote", title_prefix: title } }),

with exactly these seven consecutive lines:
  const titleResolved = title || (goal.toLowerCase().indexOf("titled ") < 0 ? "" : (goal.slice(goal.toLowerCase().indexOf("titled ") + 7).trim().split(" ")[0] ?? "").replace(/[.,;:!?]+$/, ""));
  if (!titleResolved) return null;
  try {
    const res = await fetch(`${DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT}/resolve`, {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", ...(API_KEY ? { Authorization: `ApiKey ${API_KEY}` } : {}) },
      body: JSON.stringify({ pointer: { type: "memoryNote", title_prefix: titleResolved } }),

WHY: the existing extraction of title a few lines above requires quotation marks, so an unquoted title yields an empty string, the guard returns null, and the execution receives no deterministic label and no credit even when the work was performed correctly. MEASURED BY CONTROLLED EXPERIMENT 2026-09-12 with three dispatches of the same goal form: a quoted title produced verdict achieved with notes deterministic:verified-compute-artifact recomputed 175031; an unquoted title resolved through the SAME universal-tool-fallback path produced ZERO labels while its note product-389-461 exists in the store carrying the correct value 179329; a third unquoted dispatch on a different path also produced zero labels. Execution path is therefore excluded and quotation is the cause.

WHY THESE SIX LINES TOGETHER: the guard and the use of title in the resolve call are the two places that must change, and they are not adjacent. Changing only the use site is inert because the guard returns first, and changing only the guard would let an empty title_prefix reach the resolver and could match unrelated notes. Replacing the contiguous span changes both atomically, so there is no intermediate state.

SAFETY: the fallback runs only when the quoted extraction produced nothing, so every goal that works today is unaffected. It takes the first whitespace-delimited token after the word titled and strips trailing sentence punctuation, so it cannot swallow a sentence. If the token names no note, the existing code path returns null and falls through to the remaining oracles exactly as it does today.

Do not change any other line in the file. Do not reformat the surrounding code.

POST-CONDITION: after this change the file contains the exact string titleResolved in both the guard and the title_prefix argument, the original quoted extraction of title is unchanged, and the file typechecks clean.

